  m_Name: Archaeopteryx
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  exhibitName: Archaeopteryx
  description: "The ARK Archaeopteryx is a small, bird-like creature in ARK: Survival
    Evolved that first appeared in the Late Jurassic period. In the game, it is a
    fearful, tree-dwelling carnivore that primarily eats chitin from insects. Archaeopteryx
    cannot truly fly but can glide between trees, making it an important utility
    creature for survivors. \nIn the wild, Archaeopteryx avoids the ground and flees
    when threatened. It is found in forested areas across many ARK maps, including
    The Island, Scorched Earth, Ragnarok, and Crystal Isles. Taming requires knocking
    it out (often with a Bola to immobilize it) and feeding it Simple Kibble or Chitin.
    Once tamed, it cannot be ridden but can be carried and used as an organic parachute,
    slowing a survivor\u2019s descent when held during a fall. It can also collect
    small amounts of sap when wandering near redwood trees. \n\nArchaeopteryx is
    not a combat creature but is highly valued for safe gliding and emergency falls.
    Breeding is possible, with eggs requiring an incubation temperature of 16\u201320
    \xB0C and a total maturation time of about 15.5 hours. This creature remains
    one of the most iconic utility pets in ARK for explorers navigating dangerous
    heights. "
  images: []
